  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the efficiency of Carnot&#39;s engine is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>log</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> are constants. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi></math> is temperature, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi></math> is Boltzman constant, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> is angular displacement and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> has the dimensions of length. Then, choose the incorrect option.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "H7nuA",
      "text": "Dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math> is same as that of force.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "WUEkI",
      "text": "Dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi></math> is same as that of energy.",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "aJe5b",
      "text": "Dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#951;</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math> is same as that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Cmpde",
      "text": "Dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is same as that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#951;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math>.&nbsp;Since expression inside the logarithm is dimensionless</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>&#946;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Since the dimensions of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></math>&nbsp;are equivalent to that of energy,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#946;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>E</mi></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msup><mi>MLT</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;has dimensions of force.</p><p>Since&nbsp;efficiency is a dimensionless ratio,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#946;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>0</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#946;</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced></mfrac></math></p><p>Therefore, dimensions of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;is not same as that of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>. Hence option D is incorrect statement and the answer.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#945;</mi></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>&#946;</mi></mfenced><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msup><mi>ML</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;has dimensions of energy.</p></blockquote>",
